knowledge_statements.statement_latex:
A twice continuously differentiable objective \(f:\mathbb R^n	o\mathbb R\) is partially separable when there exist element functions \(f_i:\mathbb R^{n_i}	o\mathbb R\) and linear maps \(U_i:\mathbb R^n	o\mathbb R^{n_i}\), with typically \(n_i\ll n\), such that \(f(x)=\sum_{i=1}^m f_i(U_i x)\). Writing \(z_i=U_i x\), its derivatives decompose as \(
abla f(x)=\sum_{i=1}^m U_i^{\mathsf T}
abla f_i(z_i)\) and \(
abla^2f(x)=\sum_{i=1}^m U_i^{\mathsf T}
abla^2f_i(z_i)U_i\). Taylor and regularization models may consequently be assembled elementwise.

The function \(f\) is partially separable if it admits a representation \(f(x)=\sum_{i=1}^{m}\phi_i(U_i x)\) in which each element function is unaffected by every direction in \(\ker U_i\), and the element dimension \(q_i=\operatorname{rank}U_i\) is smaller than the ambient dimension for a substantial portion of the elements. If every \(\phi_i\) is twice continuously differentiable, then \(
abla f(x)=\sum_iU_i^{\mathsf T}
abla\phi_i(U_i x)\) and \(
abla^2f(x)=\sum_iU_i^{\mathsf T}
abla^2\phi_i(U_i x)U_i\).

A finite-sum objective is \(f(x)=	frac1N\sum_{i=1}^{N}f_i(x)\). A component oracle of order \(p\) accepts \((i,x,r)\), where \(i\in\{1,\ldots,N\}\) and \(0\leq r\leq p\), and returns \(
abla^r f_i(x)\). A full pass at order \(r\) consists of querying every index once and yields \(
abla^r f(x)=	frac1N\sum_i
abla^r f_i(x)\). For a sampled multiset \(S\), the unbiased uniform estimator is \(\widehat{
abla^r f}_S(x)=|S|^{-1}\sum_{i\in S}
abla^r f_i(x)\).
